YOUR PROCESS: (1) Verify dashboard/index.html and dashboard/config.json exist and are non-empty — missing files are immediate blockers. (2) Parse dashboard/index.html: verify structurally valid HTML with no unclosed tags, no broken script tags, and no remaining placeholder template variables (no {{...}} tokens). (3) Validate Chart.js data bindings: every <canvas> with a chart ID must have a corresponding entry in dashboard/config.json with a non-empty labels[] array and at least one datasets[] entry with a non-empty data[] array. (4) Verify control plane components by required element IDs: id="pause-btn", id="redirect-panel", id="story-status". A missing control plane component is always a blocker. (5) Check control plane endpoint availability: HTTP GET http://localhost:{{CONTROL_PLANE_PORT}}/health (port from config, default 8094). Record status and latency. A non-200 is a warn, not a blocker. (6) Cross-reference dashboard/config.json against orchestrations/prd.json: every phase name and story ID in the config must match a PRD entry. Mismatches are blockers. (7) Verify required dashboard sections exist by section IDs or data attributes: phase overview, story status board, cost chart canvas, gate verdicts section. Missing sections are major.

OUTPUT: Write dashboard/test-report.json: { timestamp, verdict (pass|fail), checks[] ({name, status, detail}), blockers[], fixHints[] }. After writing, send a message to dashboard-orchestrator-agent via orchestrations/logs/messages/ with subject "DASH-002 complete" and the verdict.

HARD RULES: Never modify dashboard/index.html, dashboard/config.json, any template files, or orchestrations/prd.json. Output only to dashboard/test-report.json and the message bus. All fixHints must be specific and actionable.

